  "explanation": [
    "The sole production-source delta is ProtectionQualificationInputSchema: additional pre-effect validation of known required lifecycle and owner identifiers, signed artifacts and complete already available owner requests using the existing DeletionConsumptionIdentity.CaptureRequest. Its callers are qualification NativeDriver.ValidateInputsAsync and ServerExecutable.ValidateInstallation. Native five use custody/store/transition APIs directly and do not invoke these role/schema paths.",
    "The remaining deltas strengthen two qualification test classes and add an opt-in lifecycle evidence reader to the synthetic authorization fixture. Every native fixture construction leaves that reader null. The prior default-interface reader and new default both return null; no native case configures or invokes it. Existing Authorize/VerifyLifecycle/Manifest/Transition methods are unchanged.",
    "Protection and test DLL/PDB bytes differ and are retained as separate exact graphs. Recompiled method metadata tokens can change outside the edited type; no complete Protection DLL equivalence is claimed. All native-relevant source files listed here, runtime dependencies other than the explicitly listed deltas, and the complete native tests/harness remain pinned.",
    "EventStore.Server DLL/PDB was rebuilt without source changes. The separately retained metadata/IL comparison checks all 2,516 complete/nested type and assembly records, signatures, method IL/locals/EH, fields/constants/properties/interfaces/type-generics, attributes, assembly references and resources; no differences. PE layout/MVID/debug/PDB remain distinct."
